<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Baudh State</h1><p class="st-meta">1400 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Boudh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A princely state on the upper Mahanadi in Odisha, whose capital Boudh holds Buddhist and Hindu remains, ruled by Rajas until 1948.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tradition places the founding of the ruling dynasty around 1400. The town's name is linked to the Buddhist remains found there, including a large seated Buddha image.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Baudh was an inland state of farmland and forest on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahanadi">Mahanadi</a>. It was linked with the neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kondh">Kondh</a> hill tracts, which were separated from it under British rule in the 19th century. It paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> and later belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orissa-tributary-states">Orissa Tributary States</a>. Its internal history is poorly documented.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Baudh merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a> on 1 January 1948 and is now Boudh district, Odisha.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/baudh-state.jpg" alt="Baudh State" width="200" height="100"><figcaption>Image: User Nataraja on fr.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drapeau_Baudh.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1400 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Boudh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Odia</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Boudh</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1674&amp;focus=baudh-state" aria-label="Baudh State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6949 14